course: dictionary
lesson: 7391
title: Plurals: more than one
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Plural means more than one. «Cat» is one cat, but «cats» is more than one, so «cats» is the plural of «cat». When you talk about a group of things, the noun usually needs its plural form.
explain: Most plurals follow simple rules. Most words just add -s: dog, dogs. Words ending in s, x, z, ch or sh add -es: box, boxes. Words ending in y change it to ies: baby, babies.
explain: Some plurals break the rules, so you have to learn them. «Child» becomes «children», «mouse» becomes «mice», «foot» becomes «feet», and «sheep» stays «sheep». For a plural owner that already ends in s, add only an apostrophe: «the girls' coats» and «the teachers' room».
fact: Plural means more than one: «cats» is the plural of «cat».
fact: Add -es after s, x, z, ch or sh: «boxes» is the plural of «box».
fact: Change y to ies, as in «babies», and f to ves, as in «leaves».
fact: Irregular plurals: «children», «mice», «feet» and «sheep» do not follow the usual rules.
fact: Plural can also mean having many kinds or groups, as in «a plural society».
exercise: What is the plural of «baby»? | babyes | *babies | babys | babees
exercise: Which word is the plural of «mouse»? | mices | mouses | *mice | mousies
exercise: Which is the correct plural of «box»? | boxies | boxs | boxxes | *boxes
test: Write the plural of «leaf». | leafes | leavs | *leaves | leafs
test: Which sentence has a plural noun? | *The girls' coats hang by the door. | He is running home. | The cat sat down. | The dog barked.
exam: Which is the plural of «foot»? | *feet | feetes | foots | feets
